The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = dsps_setup_optional_vbus_irq(pdev, glue);
if (ret)
    goto err;
```
Reason:
The call to `dsps_setup_optional_vbus_irq()` is made after the platform device has been created but before it has been properly registered. If this function fails (returns an error), the error handling path does not unregister the platform device, leading to a NULL pointer dereference when the device is accessed later.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
goto unregister_pdev;
platform_device_unregister(glue->musb);
```
Reason:
The patch introduces a new error handling label `unregister_pdev` that ensures the platform device is unregistered if `dsps_setup_optional_vbus_irq()` fails. This prevents the platform device from remaining registered when it should not be, thus avoiding the NULL pointer dereference issue during subsequent accesses.

